5\n   \\]\n   Simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   v + y + kh + d + o = 20\n   \\]\n\n6. **Time for \"\u0412\u042b\u0425\u041e\u0414\"**:\n   - The letters in \"\u0412\u042b\u0425\u041e\u0414\" are \u0412 (v), \u042b (y), \u0425 (kh), \u041e (o), \u0414 (d), matching the variables in the final equation.\n\n**Final Answer**: The engraver will take \\(\\boxed{20}\\) minutes to make the plate \"\u0412\u042b\u0425\u041e\u0414\".", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. **Identify the time taken to engrave given signs:**\n   - The engraver spends a total of 50 minutes on the signs \"\u0414\u041e\u041c \u041c\u041e\u0414\u044b\" and \"\u0412\u0425\u041e\u0414\".\n   - He spends 35 minutes on the sign \"\u0412 \u0414\u042b\u041c\u041e\u0425\u041e\u0414\".\n\n2. **Analyze the signs and isolate the letters that make up the word \"\u0412\u042b\u0425\u041e\u0414\":**\n   - Consider the unique letters in \"\u0412\u042b\u0425\u041e\u0414\", which are \u0412, \u042b, \u0425, \u041e, \u0414.  \n   - Separate these letters from the letters in \"\u0414\u041e\u041c \u041c\u041e\u0414\u044b\" and \"\u0412\u0425\u041e\u0414\" to find the remaining ones:\n     - For \"\u0414\u041e\u041c \u041c\u041e\u0414\u044b\" = {\u0414, \u041e, \u041c, \u041c, \u041e, \u0414} excluding the letters V, \u042b, \u0425, \u041e, \u0414, we get the remaining letters: {\u0414, \u041e, \u041c, \u041c, \u041e, \u0414}.\n     - For \"\u0412\u0425\u041e\u0414\" = {\u0412, \u0425, \u041e, \u0414} excluding the letters from V, \u042b, \u0425, \u041e, \u0414, we get the remaining letters: {\u0414, \u041c, \u041e}.\n\n3. **Calculate the time taken to engrave the differing letters:**\n   - The letters {\u0414, \u041e, \u041c} are unique to \"\u0414\u041e\u041c \u041c\u041e\u0414\u044b\" and \"\u0412\u0425\u041e\u0414\", and as stated, their engraving time is determined by the difference in time between the two scenarios give:  \n     \\( \\text{Time difference} = 50 \\text{ minutes} - 35 \\text{ minutes} = 15 \\text{ minutes} \\).\n